From: Austin Schuh <austin.schuh@bluerivertech.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Merge :_mpn cc_library into :gmp

The previous layout split gmp into two cc_libraries:

  * :gmp     -- the core C sources (assert.c, errno.c, memory.c,
                primesieve.c, nextprime.c, rand/*.c, mpz/*.c, ...),
  * :_mpn    -- the per-arch mpn function implementations
                (assembly + generic C), which :gmp depends on.

This split has two related problems on Linux when the cc_library
boundaries become DSO boundaries or affect single-pass static linking:

1. Several per-arch .asm files reference the protected-visibility table
   `__gmp_binvert_limb_table` (defined in `mp_minv_tab.c`, which was in
   :gmp). On 32-bit ARM, `R_ARM_REL32` against an undefined protected
   symbol is a hard link error, so building the implicit `lib_mpn.so`
   for :_mpn fails with:

       ld: relocation R_ARM_REL32 against external or undefined symbol
           `__gmp_binvert_limb_table' can not be used when making a
           shared object; recompile with -fPIC
       ld: lib_mpn.so: protected symbol `__gmp_binvert_limb_table' isn't
           defined

   On x86_64 the same undefined reference is silently tolerated in the
   .so, so the breakage only shows up on ARM.

2. The generic C sources in `mpn/generic/*.c` call back into core gmp
   symbols defined in :gmp (`__gmp_init_primesieve`, `__gmp_nextprime`,
   `__gmp_tmp_reentrant_alloc/free`, `__gmp_assert_fail`, ...). With the
   split layout the static archives end up on the link line in the
   order `libgmp.a lib_mpn.a`. A single-pass linker satisfies all of
   libgmp.a's needs from libgmp.a first; when it then pulls
   `perfpow.o`, `binvert.o`, etc. out of lib_mpn.a, those objects'
   references to symbols in libgmp.a are no longer resolvable:

       ld: lib_mpn.a(perfpow.o): in function `perfpow':
           undefined reference to `__gmp_init_primesieve'
           undefined reference to `__gmp_nextprime'

The autotools build does not split mpn into its own library; everything
lives in `libgmp.a/so`. Match that layout in the Bazel build by merging
:_mpn's srcs into :gmp. :_mpn is preserved as an alias for backwards
compatibility with any downstream label references.
---
 BUILD.bazel | 28 ++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -852,7 +852,18 @@
             "scanf/*.c",
             "rand/*.c",
         ],
-    ),
+    ) + [
+        # MPN function implementations (assembly + generic C). Historically
+        # these lived in a separate :_mpn cc_library, but the resulting
+        # static-link order produces a circular reference: code in :_mpn
+        # references symbols defined in :gmp (e.g. __gmp_init_primesieve,
+        # __gmp_nextprime, __gmp_tmp_reentrant_alloc), and a single-pass
+        # linker scanning libgmp.a then lib_mpn.a leaves those symbols
+        # unresolved. Keep everything in a single cc_library so libgmp.a
+        # matches the autotools layout and a single linker pass resolves
+        # all internal references.
+        ":" + fn for fn in _ALL_MPN_FUNCTIONS
+    ],
     hdrs = [":gmp_h"],
     copts = _GMP_COPTS,
     includes = ["."],
@@ -868,22 +879,15 @@
         "rand/randmt.h",
     ],
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
-    deps = [
-        ":_gmp_hdrs",
-        ":_mpn",
-    ],
+    deps = [":_gmp_hdrs"],
 )
 
-# MPN function implementations (assembly + generic C).
-cc_library(
+# Alias kept for backwards compatibility; the MPN sources now live directly
+# in :gmp (see the comment above), but downstream users may still reference
+# the historical :_mpn label.
+alias(
     name = "_mpn",
-    srcs = [":" + fn for fn in _ALL_MPN_FUNCTIONS],
-    copts = _GMP_COPTS,
-    textual_hdrs = glob(["mpn/generic/*.c"]) + [
-        "mpn/generic/gmp-mparam.h",
-        "mpn/generic/hgcd2-div.h",
-    ],
-    deps = [":_gmp_hdrs"],
+    actual = ":gmp",
 )
 
 # =============================================================================
